# 1Password references, not secrets. `op run --env-file` resolves each op://
# URI at launch and injects the value into the process environment only — the
# key itself never lands on disk, which is the whole point of this indirection.
#
# The item lives beside the witness signing key and the Signal account
# material, in the same vault, because they are the same operational secret set
# and splitting them means one of them is eventually forgotten.
#
# Launch with:
#
#     op run --env-file deploy/tailscale/tailscale.env -- \
#       docker compose -f compose.yaml -f deploy/tailscale/compose.tailscale.yaml up -d
#
# Needed only to CREATE the node. Tailscale consumes the key at login and
# data/tailscale holds the node state from then on, so ordinary restarts never
# read this. Keys are generated reusable and ephemeral at
# https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys — ephemeral so a node that
# stops is removed from the tailnet rather than lingering as a stale entry that
# looks like a live witness.

TS_AUTHKEY=op://GDB Security/kt-witness Tailscale node authkey/credential
